# Falling branch, native 32x16 frames: resting on the trunk, rustling tell, sagging tell, falling. A crooked tan limb with
# forked twigs and violet leaves (#556: a natural shape, no animal silhouette). resting and rustle carry the at-rest cue
# (#361, D71): a pale raw-wood wedge (h) opening from the top of the joint into an ink crack, and a bunch of leaves hanging
# under the trunk side of it. That side, the leftmost 11 columns of resting, is the stub the game leaves on the trunk when
# the branch falls (FallingBranch.STUB_WIDTH), so the bunch lies wholly inside it. falling has no pale wood: it is off the trunk.
# Joint (D122, D130, 2026-11-24): the root (columns 0-5) ramps through a half step (5 6 7) into the trunk's bark (1 2 3 4)
# and flares into a collar, with no ink line down the joint. Keys 1-7 are kept out of the rim.
